    "policy": "not_detected_as_zero",
    "rationale": "iHMP's NaN are non-detects, so they become 0 (Franzosa's encoding of a non-detect on the same Broad platform) and the usual zero filter then applies: no sample lacks a whole LC-MS method (every NaN is scattered), the table holds no exact zero at all, compounds with more NaN have lower detected intensities, most of the most-missing compounds are drugs that most people do not take (furosemide, hydrochlorothiazide, sulfapyridine, gabapentin), and partly-missing compounds show a longer low tail of detected values (left-censoring at a detection limit). Masking NaN out of the loss would instead treat absence as unknown.",
